From 0714615845bf19b20079c1f6793df130842773da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:37:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [AGS] Port the input event pump (sys_events.cpp/.h) to SDL3

Phase D. The confirmed next build blocker: Engine/ac/sys_events.h:21,
fatal error: SDL_keyboard.h: No such file or directory -- the bare
SDL2-style include, plus the real event/keyboard API surface behind it.

Real signature and type changes found by reading this port's own
vendored SDL3 headers directly (vendor/SDL/include/SDL3/), not assumed:

- SDL_Keysym is removed entirely -- SDL3 flattens scancode/key(was sym)/
  mod directly onto SDL_KeyboardEvent. Every .key.keysym.* access becomes
  .key.*; sys_keysdown and ags_getkeysdown() now store/return the real
  SDL_KeyboardEvent instead of a smaller SDL_Keysym-shaped copy (SDL3
  provides no smaller equivalent struct worth introducing a parallel
  type for). is_sdl_mod_key()/make_sdl_mod_flag() move from inline (in
  the header) to declared-in-header/defined-in-cpp, since their new
  SDL_KeyboardEvent parameter type needs SDL_events.h's full definition,
  and this header deliberately avoids pulling that in (its own existing
  comment: "leads to conflicts with allegro").
- Every SDL2 event-type constant is renamed with an SDL_EVENT_ prefix
  (SDL_KEYDOWN -> SDL_EVENT_KEY_DOWN, SDL_MOUSEBUTTONDOWN ->
  SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_DOWN, etc.). SDL_WINDOWEVENT (a single type with
  a nested event.window.event sub-dispatch) is gone -- every window
  sub-event is now its own top-level SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_* type; the nested
  switch in sys_evt_process_one() flattens into more top-level cases.
  SDL_WINDOWEVENT_CLOSE -> SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_CLOSE_REQUESTED;
  SDL_WINDOWEVENT_SIZE_CHANGED -> SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_RESIZED. KMOD_* gains
  an SDL_ prefix throughout (SDL_KMOD_*).
- SDL_MouseButtonEvent/MouseMotionEvent/MouseWheelEvent's x/y/xrel/yrel
  are float now (sub-pixel precision), not int -- every read into AGS's
  int-based mouse state is now an explicit, intentional
  static_cast<int>, not an implicit truncation. SDL_MouseButtonEvent::state
  (SDL_PRESSED/SDL_RELEASED) is gone, replaced by a plain bool .down.
  SDL_MouseWheelEvent::y is now a raw float scroll amount; .integer_y
  (whole "ticks") is used instead to match the old SDL2 field's actual
  semantics, not just coerced from the new float field.
  SDL_TouchFingerEvent::fingerId was renamed fingerID (capital ID).
- SDL_GetKeyboardState() returns "const bool *" now, not "const Uint8 *".
  SDL_GetKeyFromScancode() and SDL_GetScancodeFromKey() both gained real
  new parameters (modstate/key_event, and an out-param modstate
  respectively) -- genuine signature changes, not renames.
  SDL_EventFilter's return type is bool now, not int.
  SDL_TextInputEvent::text is a heap-owned "const char *" now, not a
  fixed char[32] -- sizeof(SDL_TextInputEvent::text) (used to size a
  local buffer) would now give a pointer's size, not the old array's;
  replaced with a named constant matching the old array size (only
  ascii[0] is ever read, so this is an honest rename, not a behavior
  change). A synthetic text-input event now points .text at a
  short-lived local buffer -- confirmed safe by SDL_events.h's own doc
  comment on SDL_PushEvent: the string is deep-copied into the queue,
  the caller may dispose of it immediately after the call returns.

Also touches two files outside this patch's originally-scoped list
(PATCH-SEQUENCE.md 0017's row), both real, necessary companions to
sys_events.h's own type changes, not scope creep -- the header change
itself would otherwise break both:
- Engine/main/game_run.cpp: the same event-type-constant renames plus
  .key.keysym -> .key, in run_service_key_controls()/run_service_mb_controls().
- Engine/ac/global_game.cpp: GetPressedKeys() reads keys[i].sym -- the
  field is .key now on the SDL_KeyboardEvent ags_getkeysdown() returns.

Verified: with this patch (plus 0001-0016) applied, `make build-ags`
gets past every file this patch or its two companions touch -- no SDL2/
SDL3-related compile error remains anywhere in the build. It now fails
on a genuinely new, unrelated blocker: Engine/ac/dynobj/cc_serializer.h:22,
"'void AGSDeSerializer::Unserialize(...)' marked 'override', but does
not override" -- a fresh instance of patch 0013's int32_t-vs-int DJGPP
divergence (ICCObjectCollectionReader::Unserialize's first param is
int32_t handle; the override declared int index), in a virtual-override
shape 0013's own narrower grep (ReadArrayOfInt32/WriteArrayOfInt32 call
sites only) didn't cover. Confirmed by full build log: only 2 real
errors reported (both this one root cause), the IPO/LTO probe noise
already known harmless. Left for the next patch, not fixed here -- a
different file, different concern.
---
